  "summary": "Extends the `CheckTxInputs` unit test helper to accept transactions with multiple inputs. Adds a test case where individual inputs are within valid money ranges but their sum exceeds `MAX_MONEY`. This ensures test coverage for checking cumulative input values when verifying transactions against consensus rules.",
  "problem": "Existing `CheckTxInputs` unit tests only exercised single-input transactions, so cumulative input value `nValueIn` was always equal to individual coin value `coin.out.nValue`. Consequently, a consensus regression or mutant changing the condition `!MoneyRange(coin.out.nValue) || !MoneyRange(nValueIn)` to use logical AND would pass unnoticed.",
